vØrk on Debian and Ubuntu
=========================

This is a prototype: the network format still changes between versions,
and nothing has been audited.

What runs
---------
- The vØrk node, as a system service (`systemctl status vork`,
  `vork status`). Its configuration is /etc/vork/vork.toml, its identity
  and control socket /var/lib/vork. A new install turns on the interface
  (`tun = "vork0"`), so programs reach vØrk addresses (198.18.x.x, fd...)
  and .vork names.
- vork-net, the window and tray icon: "vØrk" in the applications menu,
  and in the tray at every login (/etc/xdg/autostart/vork-net.desktop).
  It talks to the node through its control socket.

Who may manage the node
-----------------------
root and the users in `operators` in /etc/vork/vork.toml; the user who
installed the package is put there. Others see only the node's status.
After changing the file: sudo systemctl restart vork.

First steps
-----------
    vork status               this node, its neighbors and sessions
    vork link-code            a QR code and link to link another device
    vork link 'vork-link:...' link this device to another
    vork web-link             the dashboard for a browser (needs web = ...)

More: https://github.com/vooteleaer/vork
